        "solution": "The flat starting cost is the y-intercept, b = 2. The per-mile rate is the slope, m = 1.5. So C(x) = 1.5x + 2. For a 6-mile ride, C(6) = 1.5(6) + 2 = 9 + 2 = 11. Answer: C(x) = 1.5x + 2, and a 6-mile ride costs $11."
